"it passes the field through" cannot be shown by an input whose value equals the fallback (round 107's lesson).

Three times the instrument misled me first: the extraction caught a NESTED helper's `return {` (seven keys, none
of them the report's) until it was bounded by the function body; the case used `saveCheckpoint: false`, which
skips the compile altogether, so the manifest's validation is legitimately null there; and — the one worth
